.TH ENVDIFF 1 "2026-09" "envdiff" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
envdiff \- diff environment variables between two environments, safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B envdiff
.I LEFT
.I RIGHT
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares two sets of environment variables and reports what is missing,
extra or different \(em with values masked by default, so the output can go
into a CI log or a ticket.
.PP
Each side is auto-detected:
.I file.env
for dotenv or
.BR env (1)
output,
.B \-
for standard input, and
.BI cmd: 'ssh\ prod\ env'
for the output of a command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mask
Print raw values. Careful in CI logs.
.TP
.BI \-\-ignore " REGEX"
Ignore keys matching this regular expression. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-diff
Exit 1 when the environments differ.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Output format (default text).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Compared successfully; with
.B \-\-fail\-on\-diff
they also matched.
.TP
.B 1
With
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-diff ,
they differed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Two files:
.PP
.RS
.B envdiff staging.env production.env
.RE
.PP
A local file against a remote host:
.PP
.RS
.B envdiff .env cmd:'ssh prod env' \-\-ignore '^AWS_' \-\-fail\-on\-diff
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR env (1),
.BR diff (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/envdiff
